Like Boudewijn answered, I think you're correct,
some monsters in some situations don't go extinct,
so "extinctionist" is a fuzzy concept at best.
Moreover, those cases are done that way
deliberately, apparently, that isn't a code error.
One very detailed description once posted here of an
extinctionist campaign described killing off "at
least 120" of such monsters, then, level by level
through the infected area, somehow doing "detect
monster" to assure that no randomly created ones
were being left behind, just before leaving the
level.

This does scream out a YANI, however, a command that
displays the number of monsters of each type killed
during, rather than after, the game to assure that
no class has gone short of the number needed.

Since the table-listing capability already exists in
the code to be used at the end of the game, this
should be a straightforward code change, though a
nicer one would include the zero entries too, so
that it wasn't the case that a whole class, or a
unique monster, got missed.

Would it unbalance the game in any way to be able to
check progress on extinctionist campaigns during the
game?

